 "asked_at": "2026-10-17T08:45+08:00",
 "answer": "**If you mean today in Kuala Lumpur—Saturday, October 17—first check whether your kids actually have a class or school activity scheduled.** KL’s reported Air Pollutant Index was **161 at the Cheras station at 7:00 a.m.**, in the *unhealthy* range; readings can vary by area and change through the day. ([semakapi.my](https://semakapi.my/en/kuala-lumpur?utm_source=openai))\n\nIf they **do** have school today, I’d **keep them home if they have asthma, other breathing problems, or haze-related symptoms**, especially if the activity is outdoors. For children who feel well, an indoor class with no outdoor activities may be reasonable, but it’s also reasonable to keep them home if you’re concerned—**notify the school**. Malaysia’s current guidance stops school outdoor activities above API 100 and calls for school closure at API 200; parents may choose to keep children home over health concerns if they inform the school. ([web26.bernama.com](https://web26.bernama.com/en/general/news.php?id=2620854))\n\nCheck your **school’s message and the nearest station on the official DOE APIMS** before deciding, rather than relying on a citywide reading. ([eqms.doe.gov.my](https://eqms.doe.gov.my/apims/main?utm_source=openai))",
